('advanced-native-1397', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1397-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["The strap’s stitching failed, while the zip and main compartment remained usable."],"options":["The speaker had already discarded the whole bag without asking about its strap.","The strap’s stitching failed, while the zip and main compartment remained usable.","The zip failed first, leaving a new shoulder strap as the only usable part.","The bag had never been used, and the issue was only a loose packing clip."]},"advanced-native-1397-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["The strap had worn out, but the other main parts of the bag were still usable.","The damage was in the stitching that held the load, not the zip or main compartment.","The other functions still worked, so I wanted to check a repair of the failed component before replacing the whole item.","The bag’s remaining functions gave me a reason to ask about a smaller replacement."],"options":["The strap had worn out, but the other main parts of the bag were still usable.","The damage was in the stitching that held the load, not the zip or main compartment.","The other functions still worked, so I wanted to check a repair of the failed component before replacing the whole item.","The bag’s remaining functions gave me a reason to ask about a smaller replacement."]},"advanced-native-1397-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["The initial failure did not show that the lamp had worn out; the account identifies a setup issue that was resolved."],"options":["Unlocking the switch is described as replacing a component damaged by prolonged use.","The initial failure did not show that the lamp had worn out; the account identifies a setup issue that was resolved.","The account documents years of use before the lamp stopped working."]},"advanced-native-1397-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["整件物品已沒有任何可保留或修理的部分。"],"options":["整件物品已沒有任何可保留或修理的部分。","可以詢問是哪個部件及其狀況。","有一個部件因使用而耗損。"]},"advanced-native-1397-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["The strap wore out, but I should describe that component accurately and ask about replacement before judging the whole bag."],"options":["I would judge every part from the bag’s age without checking which functions remain.","The strap wore out, but I should describe that component accurately and ask about replacement before judging the whole bag.","I thought a failed strap established that the zip had also stopped working."]},"advanced-native-1397-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["The cutting part has worn out through repeated use, leaving this ticket punch unable to make a clean hole. The wear tells us about its condition, but the surviving record does not identify an operator or an exact year.","This ticket punch wore out at its cutting edge after years of use. Its condition is visible, while the names of its operators and the exact dates of use remain unrecorded."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-1398', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1398-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["The clearing work was overlooked, then acknowledged while future cover was discussed."],"options":["The clearing work was overlooked, then acknowledged while future cover was discussed.","The volunteers had agreed to every future clearing shift before Jo spoke.","The performers alone did all the clearing after the audience left.","Jo asked for the clearing work to be removed from the acknowledgements."]},"advanced-native-1398-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["We needed to acknowledge the contribution and discuss cover, rather than assume it would continue.","We had taken the volunteers for granted instead of recognising the work after the audience left.","Our thanks had overlooked people who did essential clearing.","The end of the performance was not the end of everyone’s work."],"options":["We needed to acknowledge the contribution and discuss cover, rather than assume it would continue.","We had taken the volunteers for granted instead of recognising the work after the audience left.","Our thanks had overlooked people who did essential clearing.","The end of the performance was not the end of everyone’s work."]},"advanced-native-1398-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["Here it means assuming something is true; that is different from failing to appreciate a person’s help."],"options":["The report says the writer checked the opening with the manager before making the assumption.","Here it means assuming something is true; that is different from failing to appreciate a person’s help.","The sentence explicitly criticises the writer for not thanking the person who opens the room."]},"advanced-native-1398-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["那人已同意以後任何時間都提供相同協助。"],"options":["那人已同意以後任何時間都提供相同協助。","可以具體承認過去忽略了哪些工作。","協助的價值可能沒有得到充分重視。"]},"advanced-native-1398-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["We should not take her for granted again; thanking her past work does not tell us which future shifts she can accept."],"options":["I would use the old pattern of cover without checking whether her circumstances had changed.","We should not take her for granted again; thanking her past work does not tell us which future shifts she can accept.","I thought a more detailed thank-you could stand in for asking about her availability."]},"advanced-native-1398-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["We have taken the map for granted if we remove the names of the residents who checked it simply to enlarge a photograph. Could we keep their credit and the update date, and make the image smaller instead?","Let us not take for granted the work behind this free map. I suggest keeping the contributors’ names and update date, even if that means using a smaller photograph on the display."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-1400', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1400-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["It showed room availability, while people still had to confirm access and equipment."],"options":["The centre had decided to reject all booking information as useless.","The coordinator accepted the request before asking about access or equipment.","It showed room availability, while people still had to confirm access and equipment.","A free-room entry already confirmed a person to unlock it and all equipment to use."]},"advanced-native-1400-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["An available room did not establish that the school could enter it and use what it needed.","The record covered one part of the arrangement, leaving practical conditions to check.","People had to connect the room information with the actual opening and preparation work.","The centre cannot run on spreadsheets alone; someone still needed to confirm access and equipment."],"options":["An available room did not establish that the school could enter it and use what it needed.","The record covered one part of the arrangement, leaving practical conditions to check.","People had to connect the room information with the actual opening and preparation work.","The centre cannot run on spreadsheets alone; someone still needed to confirm access and equipment."]},"advanced-native-1400-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["Using a spreadsheet does not mean the group expects the project to run on spreadsheets alone; the account includes site checks and conversations."],"options":["Using a spreadsheet does not mean the group expects the project to run on spreadsheets alone; the account includes site checks and conversations.","The account describes a plan made entirely from the table without visiting the garden.","The spreadsheet is said to replace the conversations with the people using the space."]},"advanced-native-1400-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["表格資料在任何安排中都沒有用途。"],"options":["城市運作還需要表格分析以外的工作。","表格資料在任何安排中都沒有用途。","可以舉實際工作或人的需要來說明限制。"]},"advanced-native-1400-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["We cannot run on spreadsheets alone, but the booking data still helps when we combine it with people checking access and equipment."],"options":["I would inspect the equipment without checking whether the room had already been booked.","We cannot run on spreadsheets alone, but the booking data still helps when we combine it with people checking access and equipment.","I thought questioning reliance on the sheet meant the room dates no longer mattered."]},"advanced-native-1400-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["The service cannot run on spreadsheets alone, so could you walk us through one item from arrival to return? I would like to understand the reception, questions and teaching behind the repair total, rather than treat the number as the whole process.","Could you show how the activity works beyond its count of completed repairs, since it cannot run on spreadsheets alone? Please take one example through the conversations with its owner and the explanation given before it is returned."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-1401', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1401-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["作家成長也受到外在資料和支援影響。"],"options":["作家完全不需要自己練習。","作家成長也受到外在資料和支援影響。","作家的進步只靠天生能力。","任何回饋都保證成為名家。"]},"advanced-native-1401-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["Talent does not grow in a vacuum.","Useful feedback can help students notice what to improve.","Experienced artists can introduce unfamiliar techniques.","Support makes it easier to keep learning when a task is difficult."],"options":["Talent does not grow in a vacuum.","Useful feedback can help students notice what to improve.","Experienced artists can introduce unfamiliar techniques.","Support makes it easier to keep learning when a task is difficult."]},"advanced-native-1401-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["Her talent does not grow in a vacuum."],"options":["Her talent does not grow in a vacuum.","Her surroundings have no influence on her progress.","Her teachers do all the learning for her."]},"advanced-native-1401-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["先考慮相關資料和他人意見，再獨自在安靜房間寫報告。"],"options":["完全不問團隊需要，便定下所有安排。","先考慮相關資料和他人意見，再獨自在安靜房間寫報告。","只看單一數字，不理資料來源或參與者。"]},"advanced-native-1401-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["Curiosity does not grow in a vacuum; chances to explore can help."],"options":["Curiosity does not grow in a vacuum; chances to explore can help.","The school should select pupils who already ask questions before planning more exploration time.","Keep the opportunities unchanged and raise the curiosity target instead."]},"advanced-native-1401-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["A young cook does not grow in a vacuum; family feedback and guidance help too.","Cooking talent does not grow in a vacuum. Practice and advice from a mentor both matter."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-1402', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1402-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["好奇心提供潛能，仍需培養。"],"options":["好奇心提供潛能，仍需培養。","她已完成所有科學訓練。","有好奇心就保證研究成功。","她沒有任何可發展的長處。"]},"advanced-native-1402-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["It offers something her teachers can help develop.","It gives her raw material for further learning.","It gives her a useful starting point.","It makes her eager to ask questions."],"options":["It offers something her teachers can help develop.","It gives her raw material for further learning.","It gives her a useful starting point.","It makes her eager to ask questions."]},"advanced-native-1402-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["His speed is valuable raw material."],"options":["His speed is valuable raw material.","His speed reflects advanced technique rather than untapped potential.","His speed is mainly the result of experienced teamwork."]},"advanced-native-1402-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["已完成發展、不再需要學習的技能。"],"options":["未經進一步訓練的潛能。","已完成發展、不再需要學習的技能。","尚待培養的能力基礎。"]},"advanced-native-1402-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["Talent is raw material; practice helps shape it."],"options":["Talent is raw material; practice helps shape it.","Use the talent as evidence that the child is ready to skip the beginner exercises.","Choose harder performances first and leave technique practice until later."]},"advanced-native-1402-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["His eye for detail is raw material for photography. A course could help him develop it.","He has useful raw material in his careful observation, but he still needs to learn composition."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-1403', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1403-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["她認為創意能透過練習發展。"],"options":["她認為創意永遠無法改變。","她認為所有人的創意會以相同速度增長。","她認為練習與創意完全無關。","她認為創意能透過練習發展。"]},"advanced-native-1403-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["Yes; useful feedback can change how we work.","Yes; it can grow as we practise noticing different possibilities.","Yes; it is less like a fixed gift and more like a muscle.","Yes; regular experiments can help us find new approaches."],"options":["Yes; useful feedback can change how we work.","Yes; it can grow as we practise noticing different possibilities.","Yes; it is less like a fixed gift and more like a muscle.","Yes; regular experiments can help us find new approaches."]},"advanced-native-1403-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["Reasoning is less like a fixed gift and more like a muscle."],"options":["Reasoning cannot change after birth.","Reasoning develops at an identical rate in every learner.","Reasoning is less like a fixed gift and more like a muscle."]},"advanced-native-1403-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["能力可以發展，所以每個人必定達到完全相同水平。"],"options":["能力可以發展，所以每個人必定達到完全相同水平。","運用和練習可能提升能力。","能力不一定在出生時完全定型。"]},"advanced-native-1403-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["Think of it as less like a fixed gift and more like a muscle; small experiments may help."],"options":["Choose only tasks that already feel natural, so practice mainly confirms the talent you have.","Rank students by their first idea and use that ranking to decide who gets further practice.","Think of it as less like a fixed gift and more like a muscle; small experiments may help."]},"advanced-native-1403-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["Storytelling is less like a fixed gift and more like a muscle. Regular practice can help.","Think of storytelling as less like a fixed gift and more like a muscle that develops through practice and feedback."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-1404', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1404-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["她的英文有迅速而明顯的進步。"],"options":["她已精通所有英文用法。","她只增加練習時間，尚未見進步。","她的英文有迅速而明顯的進步。","她的英文完全沒有改變。"]},"advanced-native-1404-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["He can swim much further than before.","His technique has improved remarkably quickly.","He is far more confident in the pool now.","He has come on in leaps and bounds."],"options":["He can swim much further than before.","His technique has improved remarkably quickly.","He is far more confident in the pool now.","He has come on in leaps and bounds."]},"advanced-native-1404-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["She has come on in leaps and bounds."],"options":["She has made no noticeable progress.","She has practised longer but her performance is unchanged.","She has come on in leaps and bounds."]},"advanced-native-1404-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["長期沒有任何進步，表現一直相同。"],"options":["幾星期內見到很大進步。","能力迅速提升，表現明顯改善。","長期沒有任何進步，表現一直相同。"]},"advanced-native-1404-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["She can come on in leaps and bounds and still make mistakes."],"options":["Focus on hiding the wrong notes before comparing how much she has improved.","She can come on in leaps and bounds and still make mistakes.","She has spent more time at the piano, so I would use the phrase even without evidence of improvement."]},"advanced-native-1404-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["His signing has come on in leaps and bounds after a month of daily practice.","He has come on in leaps and bounds and can now hold a simple conversation."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-1405', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1405-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["團隊合作需要後天學習及經驗。"],"options":["說話者只在描述出生時獲得的物質資源。","團隊合作需要後天學習及經驗。","合作能力完全由出生時決定，經驗不會改變它。","說話者反對在共同任務中練習合作。"]},"advanced-native-1405-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["Good listening is not handed over at birth.","They need chances to learn how a conversation works.","Practice helps them notice when someone else wants to speak.","It takes experience to respond thoughtfully."],"options":["Good listening is not handed over at birth.","They need chances to learn how a conversation works.","Practice helps them notice when someone else wants to speak.","It takes experience to respond thoughtfully."]},"advanced-native-1405-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["These skills are not handed over at birth."],"options":["Every child already has fully developed conflict skills.","These skills are not handed over at birth.","These skills cannot improve with experience."]},"advanced-native-1405-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["它必定證明所有能力完全沒有先天差異。"],"options":["這個說法把能力想像成出生時獲分配的東西。","not handed over at birth 可用來強調需要學習。","它必定證明所有能力完全沒有先天差異。"]},"advanced-native-1405-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["Leadership is not simply handed over at birth; experience can develop it."],"options":["Leadership is not simply handed over at birth; experience can develop it.","Choose leaders mainly from the children who seemed confident from the start.","Use the first leadership task to settle which students should receive later training."]},"advanced-native-1405-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["Teamwork is not handed over at birth. Shared tasks and feedback can help us learn.","The ability to cooperate is not simply handed over at birth; it develops through working with others."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-1406', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1406-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["孩子已有不同經驗，不能當作完全一樣。"],"options":["孩子已有不同經驗，不能當作完全一樣。","所有孩子進班前都沒有任何經驗。","孩子不能再學新事物。","教師必須忽略每個孩子的背景。"]},"advanced-native-1406-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["Knowing their starting points helps us plan the lesson.","Students are not blank slates.","Their earlier experiences may affect how they understand the topic.","Some may already have useful knowledge to share."],"options":["Knowing their starting points helps us plan the lesson.","Students are not blank slates.","Their earlier experiences may affect how they understand the topic.","Some may already have useful knowledge to share."]},"advanced-native-1406-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["The pupils are not blank slates."],"options":["Their earlier experiences make further learning impossible.","The pupils are not blank slates.","The pupils have no experience that could affect learning."]},"advanced-native-1406-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["它證明所有孩子的能力及經驗必定完全相同。"],"options":["not blank slates 可以強調已有經驗。","它證明所有孩子的能力及經驗必定完全相同。","它是一種把人想像成沒有既有內容的比喻。"]},"advanced-native-1406-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["They are not blank slates; ask about their previous work first."],"options":["They are not blank slates; ask about their previous work first.","Start everyone with the same basic exercises and discuss previous experience only at the end.","Treat previous work habits mainly as something to replace before asking how they might help."]},"advanced-native-1406-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["The new members are not blank slates. Their previous experience can help us plan the workshop.","We should not treat the members as blank slates because they already use different kinds of cameras."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
